<title>GERMANY: Vegoil imports seen rising in China, Pakistan.</title>
<headline>Vegoil imports seen rising in China, Pakistan.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Joint oils and fats imports in China, Pakistan and India are set to rise to a new record in the 1996/97 (Oct/Sept) season, the Oil World newsletter said.</p>
<p>Citing Chinese and Pakistani oilseeds crop shortfalls and a stagnant figure in India, the publication put the total for the three countries at 6.33 million tonnes versus 5.52 million in 95/96 and up 200,000 tonnes from the previous high in 94/95.</p>
<p>An estimate for slightly lower Indian imports was tentative and depended on summer crops. India and China would be able to meet some of the rising demand from domestic stocks.</p>
<p>Oil World forecast net imports of 17 oils and fats in the three countries as follows (in million tonnes) --</p>
<p>							 1996/97     95/96</p>
<p>    China						3.77	2.96</p>
<p>    India						1.08	1.16</p>
<p>    Pakistan					   1.48	1.40</p>
<p>    TOTAL						6.33	5.52</p>
<p>	 of which, among other comodities --</p>
<p>    soy oil					    1.72	1.61</p>
<p>    palm oil					   3.80	3.37</p>
<p>    rape oil					   0.25	0.22</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
